{
  "version": 1,

  "_comment": [
    "Programme dashboard definitions. Copy this file to",
    "<openmrs-webapp>/WEB-INF/module-config/clinicreporting/program-indicators.json",
    "and edit the copy: the file in the module configuration directory is read in preference to this",
    "one, so a change needs no rebuild and no restart.",
    "",
    "program.uuid must be the OpenMRS programme's own UUID - find it in Administration > Manage",
    "Programs. Enrolments are matched on it, so a wrong UUID produces no figures rather than",
    "somebody else's.",
    "",
    "metric must be one of: activeEnrollments, newEnrollments, completedEnrollments,",
    "enrolledByGender, enrolledByAgeBand, enrollmentsByMonth, encounters,",
    "patientsWithObservation, observationCount, lowValueCount, averageValue,",
    "valueDistribution, positiveRate, enrolledCoverageRate.",
    "",
    "lowValueCount counts only the numeric values under the required \"valueBelow\" limit,",
    "which is what makes a low-birth-weight indicator mean low birth weight rather than",
    "every weight recorded.",
    "",
    "enrolledCoverageRate divides by the programme's active enrolment rather than by another",
    "concept, so it can read less than 100% and the gap is the people not reached. positiveRate",
    "divides by the patients with a denominator concept, and so needs \"denominatorConcepts\"",
    "naming something different from \"concepts\": a numerator equal to its own denominator",
    "divides by itself and reports 100% whatever the data says.",
    "",
    "chart may be none, bar, hbar, line or doughnut. target is optional and is the figure the",
    "indicator is measured against. higherIsBetter (default true) says which side of the target is",
    "the good one - a stock-out rate or a positivity rate is better when it is lower.",
    "",
    "Concepts are named, not hard-coded by UUID, because a concept's UUID differs between OpenMRS",
    "distributions while its name does not. Give {\"uuid\": \"...\"} when the server is known, and",
    "the name is then the fallback. An indicator whose concept this server does not have is shown as",
    "unavailable and says which concept is missing - it never reports a zero for it.",
    "",
    "Every indicator here is an aggregate. No definition can name a table or contribute SQL."
  ],

